WHAT CHANGED, AND WHAT THAT DOES NOT UNDO

Until 2026-10-01 this repository carried an MIT licence on the code and CC BY 4.0 on the
editorial content in js/data/. Those terms are withdrawn for this and all later versions.

Creative Commons licences are irrevocable for copies already distributed. Anyone who took a
copy while CC BY 4.0 was in force keeps that licence FOR THAT COPY. This file governs this
version and everything after it. At the time of the change the repository had no forks, no
stars and no watchers.

THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL KEEPS ITS OWN TERMS

Nothing here grants any right over material that belongs to somebody else. The app fetches
several things at runtime rather than committing them:

  MusicBrainz     Core data is CC0. Discographies and the shared-record lookups in
                  js/collab.js come from the MusicBrainz web service, used within its
                  rate limit. https://musicbrainz.org/doc/About/Data_License

  Wikipedia /     Portraits and biographical extracts, and film posters via the
  Wikidata        pageimages API. NOTE: the film-poster lookup uses pilicense=any, which
                  returns NON-FREE images served under fair use on Wikipedia. That is a
                  narrower permission than this project's other sources and should be
                  reviewed before any commercial use.

  Open Library /  Book cover art for the reading room, fetched and cached client-side.
  Google Books    Each cover remains the property of its publisher.

  Apple / iTunes  Thirty-second audio previews, played from their own endpoints and never
  and Deezer      copied or stored. Their API terms apply.

Biographies in js/data/ were written by a model from a fixed per-artist evidence pack and
fact-checked against it, as the "About the data" tab in Rooms describes. They are original
text and are covered by the copyright above; the facts in them are not.

Any source added later must be recorded here, with its terms, before it is used.
